      "exampleTransliteration": "adhhabu ilā l-maṭāri qabla s-sāʿati th-thālithati",
      "exampleEnglish": "I go to the airport before three o'clock.",
      "grammarNote": "قَبْلَ ('before') and بَعْدَ ('after') work exactly like تَحْتَ/فَوْقَ (level 46) — idafa-like, always followed by a genitive noun, ending in fatha because they function adverbially rather than as ordinary nouns. This example reuses the telling-time construction from level 36 (السَّاعَةِ الثَّالِثَةِ, 'the third hour' = three o'clock) to put قَبْلَ to immediate use.",
